323
00:44:09.200 --> 00:44:19.980
Drummond Reed: But because it's derived cryptographically and verifiable cryptographically, it doesn't need a centralized registry, which is where the name decentralized identifier came from, right?

324
00:44:20.300 --> 00:44:35.230
Drummond Reed: By the way, you see the term VID. At Trust Over AP, we generalized one step further and said, okay, there are various ways to do a cryptographically verifiable identifier. We don't want to say that DIDs are the only way to ever do that. So, a DID

